{"id":"hittites","name":"Hittites","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:hittites","torrey:hittites"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hittites","text":"Palestine and Syria appear to have been originally inhabited by three different tribes. (1.) The Semites, living on the east of the isthmus of Suez. They were nomadic and pastoral tribes. (2.) The Phoenicians, who were merchants and traders; and (3.) the Hittites, who were the warlike element of this confederation of tribes. They inhabited the whole region between the Euphrates and Damascus, their chief cities being Carchemish on the Euphrates, and Kadesh, now Tell Neby Mendeh, in the Orontes valley, about six miles south of the Lake of Homs. These Hittites seem to have risen to great power as a nation, as for a long time they were formidable rivals of the Egyptian and Assyrian empires. In the book of Joshua they always appear as the dominant race to the north of Galilee. Somewhere about the twenty-third century B.C. the Syrian confederation, led probably by the Hittites, arched against …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2850","lemma":"חִתִּי","xlit":"Chittîy","gloss":"a Chittite, or descendant of Cheth","kjv":"Hittite, Hittities","count":26,"share":0.55},{"strong":"H802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","xlit":"ʼishshâh","gloss":"a woman","kjv":"ess, each, every, female","count":7,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H776","lemma":"אֶרֶץ","xlit":"ʼerets","gloss":"the earth","kjv":"common, country, earth, field","count":12,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","xlit":"bath","gloss":"a daughter","kjv":"apple, branch, company, daughter","count":5,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","xlit":"ʻâlâh","gloss":"to ascend, intransitively or actively","kjv":"arise, ascend up, at once, break","count":5,"share":0.11}],"verses":["Gen.15.20","Gen.23.10","Gen.26.34","Gen.36.2","Gen.49.30","Exod.3.8","Num.13.29","Deut.7.1","Josh.1.4","Josh.9.1","Josh.24.11","Judg.1.26","Judg.3.5","1Sam.26.6","2Sam.11